<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Formal Forensic Investigation Report — {{ customer_name }}</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --ink:        #1a1a1a;
    --ink-soft:   #444;
    --line:       #d0d0d0;
    --line-soft:  #e8e8e8;
    --paper:      #fdfdfd;
    --accent:     #1f4e79;
    --highlight:  #fff3cd;
    --crit:       #c0392b;
    --high:       #d35400;
    --med:        #b7950b;
    --low:        #1f8b4c;
    --info:       #2874a6;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", Times, serif;
    color: var(--ink);
    background: var(--paper);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 880px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 56px 64px;
    font-size: 12pt;
  }
  /* Cover page */
  .cover {
    text-align: center;
    border-bottom: 3px double var(--ink);
    padding-bottom: 48px;
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }
  .cover .stamp {
    font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 9pt;
    letter-spacing: 4px;
    color: var(--crit);
    border: 1px solid var(--crit);
    padding: 4px 12px;
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .cover h1 {
    font-size: 28pt;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    font-weight: normal;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  .cover .subtitle {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 13pt;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }
  .cover-table {
    margin: 32px auto;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    text-align: left;
    font-size: 11pt;
  }
  .cover-table td {
    padding: 6px 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
  }
  .cover-table td:first-child {
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: 9pt;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
    font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
  }
  /* Section headers */
  h2 {
    font-size: 18pt;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent);
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 56px 0 16px;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  h3 {
    font-size: 14pt;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 32px 0 12px;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
    padding-left: 12px;
  }
  h4 {
    font-size: 12pt;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin: 20px 0 8px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
    font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
  }
  p { margin: 0 0 12px; }
  /* Brief / verdict box */
  .brief-box {
    background: #f9f6f0;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
    padding: 16px 20px;
    margin: 16px 0 32px;
    font-size: 11pt;
  }
  .brief-box .label {
    font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 9pt;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .verdict {
    background: #fff;
    border: 2px solid var(--ink);
    padding: 24px;
    margin: 24px 0;
  }
  .verdict.crit { border-color: var(--crit); background: #fef2f0; }
  .verdict.high { border-color: var(--high); background: #fef5ed; }
  .verdict.med  { border-color: var(--med);  background: #fefae8; }
  .verdict.low  { border-color: var(--low);  background: #eff8f1; }
  .verdict h3 {
    margin-top: 0;
    border: none;
    padding: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 16pt;
  }
  .verdict .label {
    font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 9pt;
    letter-spacing: 3px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  /* Finding block */
  .finding {
    page-break-inside: avoid;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-left: 6px solid var(--ink);
    background: #fff;
    margin: 24px 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .finding.sev-CRITICAL { border-left-color: var(--crit); }
  .finding.sev-HIGH     { border-left-color: var(--high); }
  .finding.sev-MEDIUM   { border-left-color: var(--med); }
  .finding.sev-LOW      { border-left-color: var(--low); }
  .finding.sev-INFO     { border-left-color: var(--info); }
  .finding-header {
    padding: 14px 20px;
    background: #fafafa;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .finding-header .num {
    font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 9pt;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .finding-header .title {
    font-size: 13pt;
    font-weight: 700;
    flex: 1;
  }
  .finding-header .sev-pill {
    font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 9pt;
    font-weight: 700;
    padding: 3px 10px;
    border: 1px solid;
    color: white;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
  }
  .sev-pill.sev-CRITICAL { background: var(--crit); border-color: var(--crit); }
  .sev-pill.sev-HIGH     { background: var(--high); border-color: var(--high); }
  .sev-pill.sev-MEDIUM   { background: var(--med);  border-color: var(--med); }
  .sev-pill.sev-LOW      { background: var(--low);  border-color: var(--low); }
  .sev-pill.sev-INFO     { background: var(--info); border-color: var(--info); }
  .finding-body { padding: 20px; }
  .finding-summary {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    font-size: 11pt;
  }
  /* Evidence card */
  .evidence-card {
    margin-top: 16px;
    background: #f5f5f0;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    page-break-inside: avoid;
  }
  .evidence-card .card-header {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: white;
    padding: 8px 14px;
    font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 9pt;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
  }
  .evidence-card .card-header .source { color: #ccc; font-style: italic; }
  .evidence-card .card-body {
    padding: 0;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .evidence-card table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-family: Consolas, "Courier New", monospace;
    font-size: 9pt;
  }
  .evidence-card th {
    background: #e8e4d8;
    text-align: left;
    padding: 6px 8px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 9pt;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .evidence-card td {
    padding: 5px 8px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    word-break: break-all;
  }
  .evidence-card td.highlight {
    background: var(--highlight);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .evidence-card tr:hover td { background: #f9f9f5; }
  /* Exhibit figure (rasterized tool screenshot) */
  .exhibit-figure {
    margin: 16px 0;
    page-break-inside: avoid;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .exhibit-figure img {
    max-width: 100%;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.12);
  }
  .exhibit-figure figcaption {
    font-size: 9.5pt;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-style: italic;
    margin-top: 6px;
  }
  .mono { font-family: Consolas, "Courier New", monospace; font-size: 9pt; }
  /* ATT&CK tags */
  .attack-tags { margin: 12px 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; align-items: center; }
  .attack-tags .attack-label {
    font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 8pt; letter-spacing: 1px;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-soft); font-weight: 700;
  }
  .attack-pill {
    font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 9pt; background: #eef2f7;
    border: 1px solid #c3d0df; color: #1f4e79; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 3px;
  }
  /* IOC list */
  .ioc-list {
    background: #1c1c1c;
    color: #e6e6e6;
    padding: 14px 18px;
    font-family: Consolas, "Courier New", monospace;
    font-size: 9pt;
    margin: 12px 0;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .ioc-list .label {
    color: #f0883e;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
    font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 9pt;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .ioc-list ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
  .ioc-list li { padding: 2px 0; }
  /* Conclusion / footer */
  .conclusion {
    border-top: 3px double var(--ink);
    margin-top: 56px;
    padding-top: 24px;
  }
  footer {
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 10pt;
    margin-top: 40px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
    padding-top: 16px;
  }
  /* No findings notice */
  .no-findings {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 32px;
    background: #f5f5f5;
    border: 1px dashed var(--line);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-style: italic;
  }
  /* Print */
  @media print {
    body { padding: 24px; }
    h2 { page-break-before: always; }
    h2:first-of-type { page-break-before: auto; }
    .finding { page-break-inside: avoid; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<!-- Cover Page -->
<section class="cover">
  <div class="stamp">Confidential — Investigative Material</div>
  <h1>{{ report_title }}</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Formal Forensic Investigation Report</p>
  <table class="cover-table">
    <tr><td>Customer</td><td>{{ customer_name }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Case Reference</td><td>{{ case_reference }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Investigation Date</td><td>{{ investigation_date }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Examined Host</td><td>{{ system_info.ComputerName or "N/A" }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Operating System</td><td>{{ (system_info.os_info.ProductName if system_info.os_info else None) or "Windows" }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Report Generated</td><td>{{ generated_at }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Methodology</td><td>Deterministic, automation-first (no AI inference)</td></tr>
  </table>
</section>

<!-- 1. Investigative Brief -->
<h2>1. Investigative Brief</h2>
<div class="brief-box">
  <div class="label">Reported case background</div>
  {% if investigation_prompt %}
  <p>{{ investigation_prompt }}</p>
  {% else %}
  <p><em>No specific investigation brief was supplied; this report applies the default forensic baseline (persistence, hacktools, log integrity).</em></p>
  {% endif %}
</div>

<h4>Focus Areas Determined From Brief</h4>
{% if focus_areas %}
<ul>
  {% for area in focus_areas %}
  <li><strong>{{ area.replace("_", " ").title() }}</strong> — {{ focus_descriptions.get(area, "") }}</li>
  {% endfor %}
</ul>
{% else %}
<p><em>Default focus baseline applied.</em></p>
{% endif %}

<!-- 2. Verdict -->
<h2>2. Findings Summary</h2>
{% set crit = counts.CRITICAL or 0 %}
{% set high = counts.HIGH or 0 %}
{% set med  = counts.MEDIUM or 0 %}
{% if crit > 0 %}
<div class="verdict crit">
  <div class="label">Verdict</div>
  <h3>Strong indicators of compromise / policy violation identified</h3>
  <p>{{ crit }} critical and {{ high }} high-severity finding(s) require immediate review.
     The evidence below cites the specific artifacts from which each finding was derived.</p>
</div>
{% elif high > 0 %}
<div class="verdict high">
  <div class="label">Verdict</div>
  <h3>Significant indicators identified — investigative action recommended</h3>
  <p>{{ high }} high-severity and {{ med }} medium-severity finding(s) warrant follow-up.</p>
</div>
{% elif med > 0 %}
<div class="verdict med">
  <div class="label">Verdict</div>
  <h3>Moderate indicators identified</h3>
  <p>{{ med }} medium-severity item(s) merit review in the context of the case background.</p>
</div>
{% else %}
<div class="verdict low">
  <div class="label">Verdict</div>
  <h3>No high-severity indicators detected</h3>
  <p>Within the scope of the focus areas, automation did not surface evidence of the
     activities described in the brief. This does not by itself prove the negative.</p>
</div>
{% endif %}

<table style="width:100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 16px 0;">
  <tr style="background: #fafafa;">
    <th style="padding: 8px; text-align: left; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink);">Severity</th>
    <th style="padding: 8px; text-align: right; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink);">Count</th>
  </tr>
  <tr><td style="padding:6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft); color: var(--crit); font-weight: 700;">Critical</td>
      <td style="padding:6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft); text-align: right;">{{ counts.CRITICAL or 0 }}</td></tr>
  <tr><td style="padding:6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft); color: var(--high); font-weight: 700;">High</td>
      <td style="padding:6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft); text-align: right;">{{ counts.HIGH or 0 }}</td></tr>
  <tr><td style="padding:6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft); color: var(--med); font-weight: 700;">Medium</td>
      <td style="padding:6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft); text-align: right;">{{ counts.MEDIUM or 0 }}</td></tr>
  <tr><td style="padding:6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft); color: var(--low); font-weight: 700;">Low</td>
      <td style="padding:6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft); text-align: right;">{{ counts.LOW or 0 }}</td></tr>
  <tr><td style="padding:6px 8px; color: var(--info); font-weight: 700;">Informational</td>
      <td style="padding:6px 8px; text-align: right;">{{ counts.INFO or 0 }}</td></tr>
</table>

<!-- 3. Detailed Findings -->
<h2>3. Detailed Findings &amp; Supporting Evidence</h2>

{% if not findings %}
<div class="no-findings">
  No findings produced by the deterministic engine within the configured focus areas.
  Refer to the AI-augmented technical report for additional observations.
</div>
{% endif %}

{% for f in findings %}
<div class="finding sev-{{ f.severity }}">
  <div class="finding-header">
    <span class="num">Finding {{ "%02d"|format(loop.index) }}</span>
    <span class="title">{{ f.title }}</span>
    <span class="sev-pill sev-{{ f.severity }}">{{ f.severity }}</span>
  </div>
  <div class="finding-body">
    <p class="finding-summary">{{ f.summary }}</p>
    <p>{{ f.detail }}</p>

    {% if f.attack %}
    <div class="attack-tags">
      <span class="attack-label">MITRE ATT&amp;CK</span>
      {% for t in f.attack %}<span class="attack-pill">{{ t }}</span>{% endfor %}
    </div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if f.evidence %}
      {% for ev in f.evidence %}
      {% if ev.image_path %}
      <figure class="exhibit-figure">
        <img src="{{ ev.image_path }}" alt="Exhibit {{ loop.index }}: {{ ev.title }}">
        <figcaption>Exhibit {{ loop.index }}: {{ ev.title }} — <span class="mono">{{ ev.source }}</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
      {% else %}
      <div class="evidence-card">
        <div class="card-header">
          <span>EXHIBIT {{ loop.index }}: {{ ev.title }}</span>
          <span class="source">{{ ev.source }}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>{% for h in ev.headers %}<th>{{ h }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {% for row in ev.rows %}
              <tr>
                {% for cell in row %}
                  {% set col = ev.headers[loop.index0] %}
                  <td class="{{ 'highlight' if col in ev.highlight else '' }}">{{ cell }}</td>
                {% endfor %}
              </tr>
              {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}

    {% if f.iocs %}
    <div class="ioc-list">
      <div class="label">Indicators of compromise extracted ({{ f.iocs|length }})</div>
      <ul>
        {% for ioc in f.iocs[:25] %}<li>{{ ioc }}</li>{% endfor %}
      </ul>
      {% if f.iocs|length > 25 %}<p style="color: #888; font-style: italic;">… and {{ f.iocs|length - 25 }} more (see findings.jsonl)</p>{% endif %}
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</div>
{% endfor %}

<!-- 4. Methodology -->
<h2>4. Methodology &amp; Reproducibility</h2>
<p>This report was produced by a deterministic forensic-investigation engine. No machine-learning
inference or large language model output is incorporated in any finding above; every assertion
maps directly to one or more artifact rows that the reader can independently verify by inspecting
the parsed CSV/JSONL files in the case output directory.</p>

<h4>Sources Consulted</h4>
<ul>
  <li>Windows registry artifacts (USBSTOR, Persistence, Services, Scheduled Tasks)</li>
  <li>Browser history (Chrome / Edge — via Hindsight or direct SQLite read)</li>
  <li>Execution artifacts (Prefetch, Amcache)</li>
  <li>Filesystem metadata ($MFT)</li>
  <li>LNK shortcuts in Recent</li>
  <li>Windows event logs (Security, System, PowerShell, Sysmon, etc.)</li>
</ul>

<h4>Indicator Sets Applied</h4>
<ul>
  <li>{{ stats.cloud_domains }} cloud-storage domains</li>
  <li>{{ stats.fileshare_domains }} anonymous file-sharing domains</li>
  <li>{{ stats.email_domains }} personal-webmail domains</li>
  <li>{{ stats.privacy_domains }} privacy / VPN / Tor domains</li>
  <li>{{ stats.hacktools }} known offensive-security tool names</li>
</ul>

{% if tools_used %}
<h4>Tooling Manifest</h4>
<table style="width:100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 8px 0; font-size: 10pt;">
  <tr style="background:#fafafa;">
    <th style="padding:6px 8px; text-align:left; border-bottom:2px solid var(--ink);">Tool</th>
    <th style="padding:6px 8px; text-align:left; border-bottom:2px solid var(--ink);">Role</th>
    <th style="padding:6px 8px; text-align:left; border-bottom:2px solid var(--ink);">Status</th>
  </tr>
  {% for t in tools_used %}
  <tr>
    <td style="padding:5px 8px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--line-soft); font-family:Consolas,monospace;">{{ t.name }}</td>
    <td style="padding:5px 8px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--line-soft);">{{ t.role }}</td>
    <td style="padding:5px 8px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--line-soft); color: {{ '#1f8b4c' if t.present else '#888' }};">{{ 'available' if t.present else 'not installed' }}</td>
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
{% endif %}

<h4>Evidence Handling &amp; Chain of Custody</h4>
<p>The forensic image was accessed read-only at mount point
<span class="mono">{{ evidence_source or "N/A" }}</span>. Artifacts were copied to the case
output directory and parsed with the tools listed above; original evidence was not modified.
Each exhibit in Section&nbsp;3 is reproduced from a parsed artifact whose source path is printed
in the exhibit caption, allowing independent verification against the underlying data.</p>

<!-- 5. Conclusion -->
<div class="conclusion">
  <h2>5. Conclusion</h2>
  {% if conclusion %}
    <p>{{ conclusion|replace("\n\n", "</p><p>")|safe }}</p>
  {% else %}
  <p>The above findings constitute the deterministic engine's assessment of the supplied
  forensic image against the case-specific focus areas derived from the investigative brief.
  Each numbered finding includes the supporting exhibit(s) directly extracted from parsed
  artifacts; analysts should validate each exhibit against the underlying source data and
  consider any corroborating evidence outside the scope of this automated pass.</p>
  <p>Where the AI-augmented technical report adds further observations, those are clearly
  labelled as such and may include heuristic conclusions that this deterministic report does
  not endorse.</p>
  {% endif %}
</div>

<!-- 6. Limitations -->
<h2>6. Scope &amp; Limitations</h2>
<ul>
  <li>This pass is bounded by the artifacts present on the supplied image and the focus
      areas derived from the brief; absence of a finding is not proof that an activity did not occur.</li>
  <li>Timestamps reflect the source artifact's recorded values and are subject to clock skew,
      time-zone interpretation, and anti-forensic tampering.</li>
  <li>Deterministic detections are based on curated indicator sets; novel or renamed tooling
      may evade name-based matching.</li>
  <li>Where external binaries (capa, YARA, EvtxECmd, Hayabusa) were not installed, the
      corresponding analysis was skipped — see the Tooling Manifest above.</li>
</ul>

<!-- 6b. ATT&CK coverage -->
{% if attack_techniques %}
<h2>6.1 MITRE ATT&amp;CK Techniques Observed</h2>
<p>The techniques below were tagged across the findings in this report. A Navigator
layer (<span class="mono">attack_navigator.json</span>) is written alongside this report
for import at the ATT&amp;CK Navigator.</p>
<div class="attack-tags">
  {% for tid, hits in attack_techniques %}<span class="attack-pill">{{ tid }} ({{ hits }})</span>{% endfor %}
</div>
{% endif %}

<!-- 6c. Consolidated IOC roll-up -->
{% if ioc_rollup %}
<h2>6.2 Consolidated Indicators of Compromise</h2>
<p>De-duplicated indicators aggregated across all findings (full export:
<span class="mono">ioc_rollup.json</span>).</p>
{% for typ, vals in ioc_rollup.items() %}
<h4>{{ typ|upper }} ({{ vals|length }})</h4>
<div class="ioc-list"><ul>
  {% for v in vals[:60] %}<li>{{ v }}</li>{% endfor %}
</ul>{% if vals|length > 60 %}<p style="color:#888;font-style:italic;">… and {{ vals|length - 60 }} more</p>{% endif %}</div>
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

<!-- 7. Glossary -->
<h2>7. Glossary</h2>
<table style="width:100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 10pt;">
  <tr><td style="padding:4px 8px; font-weight:700; width:170px; vertical-align:top;">Amcache</td>
      <td style="padding:4px 8px;">Registry hive recording program-execution metadata, including SHA-1 of executed binaries.</td></tr>
  <tr><td style="padding:4px 8px; font-weight:700; vertical-align:top;">Prefetch</td>
      <td style="padding:4px 8px;">Windows execution-acceleration files that evidence which programs ran and when.</td></tr>
  <tr><td style="padding:4px 8px; font-weight:700; vertical-align:top;">Shellbags</td>
      <td style="padding:4px 8px;">Registry records of folders a user browsed in Explorer, surviving deletion of the folder.</td></tr>
  <tr><td style="padding:4px 8px; font-weight:700; vertical-align:top;">USN Journal</td>
      <td style="padding:4px 8px;">NTFS change journal recording file create/rename/delete operations.</td></tr>
